# The common-action conclusions of source 11.3.7

`source_action_complete` proves all five clauses under the permitted exact
preceding-source inputs. The literal action kernel is O₂(K), its quotient
action is faithful, and K-star has the same concrete PSL₂ identification.
The actual Hall geometry gives D₀ ≤ L and a Cartan containing D₀.

Local uniqueness eliminates the left fixed spaces; B.5.1(3) supplies copies
of the original chosen natural action on ⟨Z^L⟩. Their common Cartan scalar
proves the whole omega-center dichotomy and eliminates C_{V_H}(K), including
the doubled SL₃ case. The scalar spectrum then gives the original line
commutator, and reciprocal transvections identify the selected conjugate
with V and its actual star image with a residual Sylow subgroup.

The older conditional and single-module interfaces are preserved. Final
assembly with the preceding §§11.0--11.2 and 11.3.4--6 source conclusions
remains with qt-d-1222-shadow-common-core.
-/
